WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.540
A meadow, with two
counters: one for rabbits,

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:04.950
one for foxes.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.420
More rabbits feed more foxes.

4
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.670
More foxes eat more rabbits.

5
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.700
Then fewer rabbits starve the foxes.

6
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.640
The numbers chase each other.

7
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.020
Where does it all end?

8
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.400
A steady balance?

9
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.470
Does one species die out?

10
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.390
In this mission, you'll
model a coupled system,

11
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.240
where each rate depends
on both quantities.

12
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.000
You'll step it forward
in small steps of time,

13
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.910
one after another, using Euler's method.

14
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.990
And you'll plot foxes
against rabbits as a path:

15
00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.480
a phase portrait.

16
00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.080
Your mission: decide where
the foxes and rabbits end up.
